WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.970
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:12.070
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:17.650
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:26.420
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.160
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.630
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.500
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.240
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.900
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.580
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.580 --> 00:01:01.250
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.630
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:12.270
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:17.170
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:22.410
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:32.520
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:37.260
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:41.990
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.860
What's this key for?

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.370
At precisely 2:30 by my
watch, the bomb will explode.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.970
Where is the tape?

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:57.100
I mailed it to myself.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:00.270
It should arrive around 2:00 pm today.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:01.670
Let them get the tape;

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:04.240
let's remove the bomb
around your neck first!

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:07.110
There's no point to this match
unless it's a complete victory.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.280
So the tape comes first.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.950
<i>You rush straight for the tape,
Kosuke-kun.</i>

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.450
Leave it to me!

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.450
<i>You're not thinking
that it's okay for you to die</i>

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.220
<i>as long as I'm saved?</i>

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:22.530
Unlike my brother, I'm a fool.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:25.790
I have to be,
or else I can't protect anyone.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:30.790
"The Only Clear Option"

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.740
<i>"The power to believe...</i>

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:46.300
<i>...can change even fate."</i>

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.330
-Are you listening?
-Yes.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.360
Don't worry.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:09.330
There's a way for me to survive.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.840
She said she has a detonation device.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:15.170
If so, then she must have
a shut-off switch, too.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:17.980
She probably at least has a spare key.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:19.940
I'm going to bet on it.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.710
Bet? What are you going to do?!

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:24.720
Going to create a situation
in which she'll die too

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.180
if she doesn't disarm the bomb.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.420
Isn't that...

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:30.420
I'm hanging up now.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:33.790
I'll call again.
Just sit tight and don't worry.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:36.530
<i>Narumi-san...</i>

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.090
Miss!

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.470
Oh, right!

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.600
<i>Don't die, Narumi-san!</i>

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:55.880
<i>Without the key, his last
hope is my shut-off switch.</i>

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:00.580
<i>He'll try to create a situation
to make me press this.</i>

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:04.820
<i>A situation in which I'll
die too if I don't press it.</i>

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:05.660
<i>To accomplish that,</i>

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:09.620
<i>he would need to increase the
effective range of that miniature bomb.</i>

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:13.430
<i>By lighting a large amount of
kerosene or gasoline on fire</i>

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.920
<i>when the explosion occurs!</i>

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.640
<i>Naturally, his possible
locations would be limited.</i>

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.910
<i>A place with nobody around.</i>

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:31.620
<i>A place near Shumari Station,
in case he failed to get the key.</i>

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.450
<i>The only such place in town...</i>

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:37.320
<i>...is the area around this bridge.</i>

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:41.530
<i>Before the game started,</i>

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:44.980
<i>he must have hidden it
around here somewhere.</i>

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:16.920
<i>Timely mailman, I owe you one.</i>

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.040
<i>To avoid being seen by anyone,</i>

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.400
<i>I have only 10 seconds...</i>

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.600
<i>Sorry, Little Narumi.
The tape is...</i>

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:58.300
What the?!

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:00.970
Yeah, sorry 'bout that!

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:05.580
I sent a bunch of dummies
to confuse you.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.480
Pretty sweet, huh?

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:08.410
Dummies?

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:12.380
<i>Though there is one little problem.</i>

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:13.920
What?

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.410
I can't tell which
is the real one, either.

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:22.990
I did a really good job making them,
if I do say so myself.

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:25.230
What are you admiring them for?!

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.100
<i>Are you even trying to play?!</i>

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:29.700
I guess there's no other choice.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:33.070
Opening them one by one
is the only way...

00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:37.170
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:40.110
<i>Talk about a real blockhead!</i>

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:45.270
You should never let
your guard down. Y'know?

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:54.750
Hi ho, Silver...away!

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.860
Come back here, you dirty bike thief!

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:02.800
<i>Phase 1 complete.</i>

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:06.240
<i>Now to see if I can get this off.</i>

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:19.910
<i>I'll call again.
Just sit tight and don't worry.</i>

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:24.050
<i>Yes, I'm waiting...</i>

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:28.620
<i>But I'm still going to worry.</i>

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:34.260
Sorry, Rio! He got the tape!

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:37.570
Hello?

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:40.270
<i>You're so stupid, Kosuke-kun!</i>

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:41.270
Alright.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.710
Go to Shumari Station.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:45.410
<i>There's a chance Hiyono-san
might be able to return</i>

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:47.110
at the very last minute.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:49.380
-What about the tape?!
-Don't worry.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:51.310
It's coming to me.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:55.320
So we have a chance...

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:58.320
But be careful.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:01.060
Even though he's putting
his life on the line,

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:03.080
he laughed like it was nothing.

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:07.320
<i>That's the Kiyotaka-sama in him.</i>

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:10.200
Want backup?

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:12.460
I'd prefer it to be 1-on-1
at the very end.

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:14.770
And besides,

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:20.070
Little Narumi is already
as good as dead.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.890
<i>-Narumi-san?!
-Yo.</i>

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:33.820
Don't give me "Yo"!

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.730
Listen! I'm at Uchiyama Station
right now!

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:38.830
The train that will get
back there the soonest

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:41.270
is the high speed express train at 2:16!

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:44.570
It arrives at Shumari Station
just before 2:30.

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:48.110
If I can get you the key as the train
is sliding into the platform,

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:49.770
we'll make it in the nick of time!

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:50.640
Out of the question.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:53.110
Asazuki is staked out at the station.

00:08:53.110 --> 00:08:55.650
Stop making decisions.

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:57.280
What do you mean
stop making decisions?!

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:59.440
-I'm trying to help you...
-I know.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:04.290
But just do what I say.

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:07.320
-Okay?
-Okay.

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:08.380
The plan is this...

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:14.960
...that's how it'll go.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:17.400
Understood.

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.430
<i>-Later...
-Narumi-san?!</i>

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:23.270
Be careful...

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:24.430
Yeah...

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:28.710
Now then...

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:34.740
The very last second
will decide this match.

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:41.990
What is it?

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:43.530
Can we meet?

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:45.830
You want me to remove the bomb?

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:48.300
You want the tape, don't you?

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:53.060
Where do we meet?

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:03.010
<i>This time I'll come out swinging!</i>

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:05.650
<i>Sad as it is,</i>

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:09.110
<i>that's the only way to change our fate...</i>

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:17.630
<i>Thanks to the pain,
my senses are sharper.</i>

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:21.130
<i>It's actually an advantage,
not a handicap.</i>

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:25.190
<i>Little Narumi,
you have no way of winning.</i>

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:32.940
Looks like we've passed
the 10 minute mark.

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:38.980
You're right.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:57.000
Looks like we've passed
the 10 minute mark.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.640
You're right.

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:00.900
I better hurry it up before I die.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:05.140
You're looking for this, I take it?

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:08.380
So you brought it? Thanks a bunch.

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:10.480
I absolutely will not press it for you.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.220
You're going to die.

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:16.620
No, I absolutely will not die.

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:22.290
Kerosene. I'll burn pretty good
if I explode.

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:24.900
As will this...

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:29.530
You won't be satisfied if you
don't get both my head and the tape.

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:31.700
Unless you use that shut-off switch,

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:32.970
you will die.

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:37.500
Or more technically, your pride will.

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:40.140
You're right.

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:42.810
<i>Assuming it is filled with kerosene.</i>

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:45.350
I replaced it with water.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:48.320
All that you're going to get...

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:49.980
...is death.

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:55.690
After your head is blown off,

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:58.330
I'll be taking the tape
from your corpse.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:00.630
That will ensure my complete victory...

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:03.770
You can have it if you want.

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:05.270
It's a dummy.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:07.840
The real one's still in my mailbox.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:12.340
All I did was show Asazuki
a pre-prepared package.

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:16.070
You guys misunderstood and
thought I recovered the real one.

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:20.280
Asazuki is at Shumari Station, right?

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.950
<i>But Hiyono-san won't
appear at the station.</i>

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:25.690
Because she's not on her way
to give you the bomb key,

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:27.190
but to get the tape instead...

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:30.590
That's right. I instructed her
to take a taxi.

00:12:30.590 --> 00:12:33.360
She should get there
by 2:40 at the latest.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:35.520
Even if you sent him now
he wouldn't make it in time.

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:38.400
<i>You're the ones who lost.</i>

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.540
<i>No way!</i>

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:43.530
<i>Was I manipulated just as he wanted?!</i>

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:46.470
You didn't realize it?

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:48.580
Probably not.

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:52.650
I made rescuing her my
priority over everything else.

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:54.380
You failed to gauge that.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:02.430
Very well.

00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:04.660
In regards to the tape, I admit defeat.

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:07.260
Things will get sticky
if the police get it,

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.200
but I'll accept that risk.

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:12.200
<i>However, even if you were
able to protect Hiyono-san,</i>

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:14.910
you cannot escape your death!

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:16.840
You think?

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:19.910
I anticipated that the container's
contents would be replaced.

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:21.950
I was never depending on it at all.

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:23.110
You're all talk...

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:25.220
I already told you.

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:27.120
I won't die.

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:29.090
The last 3 minutes.

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:31.520
I'll let you witness a miracle.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:33.190
A miracle?!

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:37.730
Here. You handle the countdown.

00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:41.630
<i>Little Narumi has
no chance left at all.</i>

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:45.800
<i>There can't be any miracle!</i>

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:48.710
You think there's no chance left,
do you?

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:51.810
There are still two ways to survive.

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:54.810
Your bluffs are getting lame, you know.

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:57.810
One is that you use
your shut-off switch.

00:13:57.810 --> 00:13:59.750
Completely out of the question!

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:01.690
I would never do
anything that pathetic!

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:04.150
Then why are you looking
after it so carefully?

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:09.260
Wouldn't breaking it or
getting rid of it be better?

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:11.860
You're confused.

00:14:11.860 --> 00:14:14.230
You're not sure if it's okay
to kill me or not.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:19.340
Right now, I have absolute faith
that I won't die.

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:21.440
There's no logic or anything to it.

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:24.100
Just simple, unwavering faith.

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:27.510
I believe my brother once said it...

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:31.280
"The power to believe
can change even fate..."

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:33.780
Let's see, then!

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:36.780
Am I the kind of person
to die in a place like this?!

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:42.760
<i>The one holding
Little Narumi's life is me...</i>

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:44.190
<i>Me!</i>

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:49.670
<i>The happiness of those who believe...</i>

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:55.370
<i>Is he really the key
to saving the Blade Children?</i>

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.470
<i>"Calm down. Just wait for the time."</i>

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:05.420
<i>We have almost no time left...</i>

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:08.910
<i>We're living on the very edge!</i>

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:12.120
<i>Kiyotaka!</i>

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.830
I won't press it! I've made up my mind!

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:21.030
Even if the results
are the worst possible,

00:15:21.030 --> 00:15:22.600
I will not press it!

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:25.170
Many times have I suffered
and felt about to die,

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:28.000
yet I've always had my way.

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:31.270
I won't bend to something
this insignificant!

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:36.710
Then that leaves one way left.

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:38.620
There is no other way!

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:39.950
No...

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:42.290
...there is.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:45.190
If this thing doesn't explode.

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:51.130
Are you insane?
That would never happen...

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:53.030
Are you so sure?

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:55.300
Machines and malfunctions
go hand-in-hand.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:57.470
I'm the one who made that.

00:15:57.470 --> 00:15:58.200
Not in a million years...

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:02.400
Then in a billion years it
might malfunction.

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:06.510
<i>It could never happen.</i>

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:07.770
<i>But...</i>

00:16:08.810 --> 00:16:13.720
<i>But Kiyotaka-sama could probably
summon forth such a fluke.</i>

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:19.710
<i>With his strong luck, he could
make it happen out of necessity...</i>

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:25.290
<i>If so, then could his
little brother do the same?</i>

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:28.890
How much time?

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:33.770
I think we've passed
the one-minute mark now.

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:36.510
To be honest, I don't really
know what you guys want

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:38.780
or what my brother is thinking.

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:43.410
But the one certain thing is
that I'm being tested for something.

00:16:43.410 --> 00:16:44.540
Isn't that right?

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:49.150
Well, then.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:51.750
Let us welcome the
moment of truth together.

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:55.150
Ten seconds left.

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:58.430
I absolutely will not press it!

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:01.100
Calm down and just count.

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.170
Seven seconds. Six...

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:06.500
Five...Four...Three...

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:07.700
Two...

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:09.340
One!

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:10.360
Zero!

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:24.720
No way...

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:26.480
What dumb luck!

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:29.830
I'm surprised too.

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:33.060
This great luck,
it's almost like my brother's.

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:39.170
<i>My resoluteness...my calculations...</i>

00:17:39.170 --> 00:17:41.500
<i>Did they lose to dumb luck?</i>

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:44.910
<i>I refuse to accept this!</i>

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:49.370
<i>But time doesn't lie...</i>

00:17:49.950 --> 00:17:51.110
<i>Time?!</i>

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:52.510
Stay back!

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:56.080
<i>I thought so!</i>

00:17:56.890 --> 00:18:00.320
You kept talking to me with
your excessive confidence

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:03.320
to confuse me and numb
my sense of time...

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.570
This watch is 2 minutes fast.

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:12.570
It was only natural that the bomb
didn't explode when it said 2:30.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:15.810
You intended to take advantage
of my delusion of defeat

00:18:15.810 --> 00:18:17.970
to steal the shut-off device...

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:19.810
Impressive.

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:24.150
<i>You truly are worthy of being
Kiyotaka-sama's younger brother.</i>

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:25.820
But I win!

00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:28.610
I saw through you and won!

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:37.660
Now your death has been sealed.

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:42.030
10 more seconds
and I could've stolen it...

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:44.000
You realized it too quickly.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:45.590
So sorry.

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:52.700
Why can't I ever be like my brother?

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:57.510
One minute left.

00:18:57.510 --> 00:18:59.000
I see...

00:19:02.650 --> 00:19:05.690
I guess I can only pray now...

00:19:05.690 --> 00:19:11.030
I beseech you, O' Lord!
Save this pitiful sinner!

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:13.190
There's no such thing as God.

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:15.730
Are you so sure?

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:19.540
Look...

00:19:19.540 --> 00:19:21.970
A goddess has arrived!

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:32.580
<i>If it's the train arriving at
Shumari Station right before 2:30,</i>

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:36.590
<i>then it will pass by
this bridge even sooner.</i>

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:41.290
<i>If he was lying about Hiyono-san
going to get the tape, then!</i>

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:44.490
My prayer has been heard!

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:46.720
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:19:58.110 --> 00:19:59.870
Hallelujah!

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:14.120
Disarm successful!

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:20.090
I thought I was a goner for sure!

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:26.570
Welcome back.

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:29.240
<i>Why hello there, Asazuki-san.</i>

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:31.800
<i>Narumi-san won!</i>

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:35.210
Were you...

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:39.580
Were you betting on that
moment from the very start?

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:40.820
Yeah.

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:43.820
The gas container, the tape
recovery, the fancy act...

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:46.760
It was all meant to blind you,
nothing more.

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:49.420
To be honest, I was really
nervous that you would notice.

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:54.660
My brother would've
won much more stylishly,

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:56.930
but this was my all.

00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:04.040
I'm never doing this
sort of thing again...

00:21:05.770 --> 00:21:11.470
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:18.170
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:36.330
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:41.970
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:41.970 --> 00:21:47.880
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:54.450
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.450 --> 00:22:00.190
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.190 --> 00:22:05.390
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.390 --> 00:22:11.230
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.230 --> 00:22:22.840
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:28.620
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:34.920
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:39.010 --> 00:22:42.650
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:42.650 --> 00:22:43.920
Security is the greatest enemy,

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:45.690
a change in the wind
changes the situation,

00:22:45.690 --> 00:22:47.820
the mountain is unmoving
before the wind!

00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:54.100
Next episode is proof that
good things come to those who wait.

00:22:54.100 --> 00:22:56.460
On the next Spiral:
Bond of Reasoning...

00:22:56.460 --> 00:22:58.470
Goodnight, Sweetheart

00:22:58.470 --> 00:23:03.100
Incidentally, I can fall asleep
right away, anytime, anywhere!

00:23:03.100 --> 00:23:04.590
That's all for today's
Hiyono's Playhouse!

00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:08.040
What the heck are you doing?!
